WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.334 --> 00:00:03.067
-Raymond Lee, welcome to
"The Tonight Show."

00:00:03.067 --> 00:00:04.067
Thanks for coming on.

00:00:04.067 --> 00:00:05.400
-Thank you so much
for having me.

00:00:05.400 --> 00:00:07.267
This is a dream come true.
I'm so excited to be here.

00:00:07.267 --> 00:00:08.968
-Oh, you're a good man.
Come on, this is --

00:00:08.968 --> 00:00:10.901
[ Cheers and applause ]
You had a great year.

00:00:10.901 --> 00:00:13.467
Not only are you starring in the
big new show, "Quantum Leap,"

00:00:13.467 --> 00:00:16.234
you also were in
"Top Gun: Maverick."

00:00:16.234 --> 00:00:17.501
Look at this right there.

00:00:17.501 --> 00:00:20.868
-Yeah, there's Miles
and there's my buddy, Jake.

00:00:20.868 --> 00:00:22.334
And there's Manny.
-Yeah.

00:00:22.334 --> 00:00:23.634
-Yeah.
-Not too shabby, huh?

00:00:23.634 --> 00:00:24.834
-Not too shabby.

00:00:24.834 --> 00:00:26.968
-What is the audition process
like for this?

00:00:26.968 --> 00:00:30.667
-Well, I thought --
I thought my read went okay.

00:00:30.667 --> 00:00:33.868
But I had just gotten back
from a trip to Hawaii,

00:00:33.868 --> 00:00:35.501
where I rented a surfboard.

00:00:35.501 --> 00:00:38.667
And I went out,
and about five minutes into

00:00:38.667 --> 00:00:40.300
paddling -- It was low tide.

00:00:40.300 --> 00:00:41.667
The reef was exposed.
-Yeah.

00:00:41.667 --> 00:00:44.901
-And, so, I'm getting out there
and I realize that I felt

00:00:44.901 --> 00:00:47.000
a sharp pain in my right hand.

00:00:47.000 --> 00:00:49.133
And I had slapped a sea urchin,

00:00:49.133 --> 00:00:50.934
and there was
about 50 spikes in my hand.

00:00:50.934 --> 00:00:53.400
And at that point, I decided
I could do one of two things.

00:00:53.400 --> 00:00:55.300
I could paddle back to shore
and just eat

00:00:55.300 --> 00:00:58.100
the cost of the surfboard that
I've had for about five minutes

00:00:58.100 --> 00:01:01.434
or I could just go out
and keep surfing, and I did.

00:01:01.434 --> 00:01:03.868
And it was --
It turned out to be a great day.

00:01:03.868 --> 00:01:06.067
I had a bloody hand.
but I came back,

00:01:06.067 --> 00:01:08.534
and the very next day was
the audition for "Top Gun."

00:01:08.534 --> 00:01:10.534
And I had a bandaged hand.
They had asked me about it.

00:01:10.534 --> 00:01:12.868
So, I thought my read went okay.

00:01:12.868 --> 00:01:15.367
But it was that story, I think,
is what sold them,

00:01:15.367 --> 00:01:19.234
because here they was
trying to cast a pilot,

00:01:19.234 --> 00:01:20.534
a daredevil pilot.

00:01:20.534 --> 00:01:22.501
And here I was,
I did something daredevilish.

00:01:22.501 --> 00:01:24.100
And maybe they were like...

00:01:24.100 --> 00:01:25.100
-"Oh, he's got something
right there." Yeah.

00:01:25.100 --> 00:01:26.734
-..."Yeah, he's got something.

00:01:26.734 --> 00:01:28.133
He took a risk."

00:01:28.133 --> 00:01:31.100
-"He took the risk."
He got a bloody hand.

00:01:31.100 --> 00:01:32.434
-Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:01:32.434 --> 00:01:35.000
Did your family freak out that
you were in "Top Gun"

00:01:35.000 --> 00:01:36.767
or that you're in billboards
all over the place?

00:01:36.767 --> 00:01:38.634
-Yeah, totally.
-They love it.

00:01:38.634 --> 00:01:40.934
-They love it, yeah.
-Look at this billboard ad here.

00:01:40.934 --> 00:01:42.234
-It's so big.
-I like this ad.

00:01:42.234 --> 00:01:43.434
This is you, basically, leap--

00:01:43.434 --> 00:01:45.334
quantum-leaping
through a building.

00:01:45.334 --> 00:01:46.834
-Yeah.
-A giant, giant building.

00:01:46.834 --> 00:01:48.234
-A huge building.
-Yeah.

00:01:48.234 --> 00:01:52.968
-Yeah, they're really proud.
-Yeah, good. They should be.

00:01:52.968 --> 00:01:54.734
-They're -- Yeah,
they're really supportive.

00:01:54.734 --> 00:01:58.000
They've always been
very supportive.

00:01:58.000 --> 00:02:00.834
I got a call from my uncle,

00:02:00.834 --> 00:02:04.033
who is very withholding
in terms of any term --

00:02:04.033 --> 00:02:07.367
like, words of congratulations
or praise or anything,

00:02:07.367 --> 00:02:09.901
but he told me that,
"I'm very proud of you."

00:02:09.901 --> 00:02:11.000
He said,
"I'm very proud of you."

00:02:11.000 --> 00:02:12.400
I got very emotional.

00:02:12.400 --> 00:02:14.567
-Yeah, and he doesn't
normally give you praise.

00:02:14.567 --> 00:02:15.801
-He doesn't normally
give me praise.

00:02:15.801 --> 00:02:17.200
And I asked him.

00:02:17.200 --> 00:02:20.067
I was like, "Is this because
I was in an ad or is this --

00:02:20.067 --> 00:02:21.367
Did you watch the episode?"

00:02:21.367 --> 00:02:24.567
He's like, "No. You were in
the Korean newspaper."

00:02:24.567 --> 00:02:27.834
And for us, if you make
the Korean newspaper,

00:02:27.834 --> 00:02:30.834
that is all
that really matters, so...

00:02:30.834 --> 00:02:32.601
-And then here's what I love
is that he actually

00:02:32.601 --> 00:02:34.000
sent you the newspaper of you.

00:02:34.000 --> 00:02:35.167
-He sent it to me.

00:02:35.167 --> 00:02:37.400
He's like, "This is what
I'm reading right now,

00:02:37.400 --> 00:02:38.467
and I'm so proud of you."

00:02:38.467 --> 00:02:41.167
And that's that.
-Come on, buddy.

00:02:41.167 --> 00:02:42.501
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:45.701 --> 00:02:46.734
That's fantastic.

00:02:46.734 --> 00:02:48.300
Uncle, he's doing pretty well,

00:02:48.300 --> 00:02:49.767
so, yeah, you don't have to
worry about him.

00:02:49.767 --> 00:02:51.934
Yeah, he's doing alright.

00:02:51.934 --> 00:02:54.501
I've got to say,
"Quantum Leap" --

00:02:54.501 --> 00:02:56.868
This is a big, exciting thing
for "Quantum Leap" fans.

00:02:56.868 --> 00:02:58.033
You must have been a baby when

00:02:58.033 --> 00:03:00.300
the first "Quantum Leap"
came out.

00:03:00.300 --> 00:03:02.667
Yeah, it wasn't a show that
you watched growing up, right?

00:03:02.667 --> 00:03:03.767
-Yeah, no.

00:03:03.767 --> 00:03:06.801
I watched it
the second time around,

00:03:06.801 --> 00:03:08.267
when it was in syndication.

00:03:08.267 --> 00:03:10.501
It was my best buddy
in sixth grade --

00:03:10.501 --> 00:03:11.801
this was his favorite show.

00:03:11.801 --> 00:03:13.267
David Kelegian,
if you're out there,

00:03:13.267 --> 00:03:15.767
thank you so much for
introducing me to the show,

00:03:15.767 --> 00:03:17.334
because prior to that,
it was just, like,

00:03:17.334 --> 00:03:19.467
cartoons and "Ninja Turtles."

00:03:19.467 --> 00:03:20.801
-Yeah, what children
should watch.

00:03:20.801 --> 00:03:23.100
Yeah, yeah. Of course.
-And then he introduced me --

00:03:23.100 --> 00:03:24.534
-Yeah, you shouldn't be
watching "Quantum Leap"

00:03:24.534 --> 00:03:25.767
as a child, as a baby.

00:03:25.767 --> 00:03:26.767
No, no, no, no.
-No.

00:03:26.767 --> 00:03:27.968
-You watch cartoons, yeah,

00:03:27.968 --> 00:03:29.501
and then you grow up to be
in "Quantum Leap."

00:03:29.501 --> 00:03:30.667
-That is right.
-Exactly what you did.

00:03:30.667 --> 00:03:33.767
-Come full circle.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:33.767 --> 00:03:36.033
-Can we set up the show
and who you play?

00:03:36.033 --> 00:03:38.934
-Yeah. It's been
30-some-odd years since

00:03:38.934 --> 00:03:41.167
Dr. Sam Beckett stepped into
the quantum accelerator

00:03:41.167 --> 00:03:42.734
and vanished forever.

00:03:42.734 --> 00:03:44.968
And now, a new team
has been assembled

00:03:44.968 --> 00:03:48.601
to restart this machine and
uncover the mysteries behind it.

00:03:48.601 --> 00:03:51.634
I am part of that new team.
I play Dr. Ben Song.

00:03:51.634 --> 00:03:54.033
And I have taken
an unsanctioned leap

00:03:54.033 --> 00:03:56.033
into the past
for reasons unknown.

00:03:56.033 --> 00:03:58.100
And my team
is left to figure out why

00:03:58.100 --> 00:03:59.534
and to try and bring me back.

00:03:59.534 --> 00:04:01.734
-Monday nights, 10:00, NBC.

00:04:01.734 --> 00:04:04.567
I will say I heard this --

00:04:04.567 --> 00:04:06.334
that, you know,
you were a little nervous

00:04:06.334 --> 00:04:08.767
when you're the number 1,
you know, on the call sheet.

00:04:08.767 --> 00:04:09.968
You have to go to set.

00:04:09.968 --> 00:04:12.434
And to calm you down,
you will sing a song.

00:04:12.434 --> 00:04:13.667
-I do.

00:04:13.667 --> 00:04:15.534
-Yeah. Do you know what song
I'm talking about?

00:04:15.534 --> 00:04:19.667
-I know what song
you're talking about. Yeah.

00:04:19.667 --> 00:04:22.167
It's a song by Hoobastank.

00:04:22.167 --> 00:04:23.300
-Okay.

00:04:23.300 --> 00:04:25.400
-Yeah, and to calm my nerves --

00:04:25.400 --> 00:04:28.234
You know,
I don't like awkward silences.

00:04:28.234 --> 00:04:30.400
Like, I don't like sonic voids.

00:04:30.400 --> 00:04:32.734
And so I just -- I hum things.

00:04:32.734 --> 00:04:36.667
And this is -- this is --
So, right now,

00:04:36.667 --> 00:04:40.734
it's pretty quiet,
so I'm getting pretty nervous.

00:04:42.267 --> 00:04:47.167
♪ I'm not a perfect person ♪

00:04:47.167 --> 00:04:49.167
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:51.667 --> 00:04:54.934
♪ There's many things I wish
I didn't do ♪

00:04:54.934 --> 00:04:56.601
Sometimes, like,
the crew that I'm working with

00:04:56.601 --> 00:04:58.501
likes to join in at this part
or they just wait until

00:04:58.501 --> 00:05:01.267
the chorus, because everyone
eventually starts to sing.

00:05:01.267 --> 00:05:05.167
♪ But I continue learning ♪

00:05:05.167 --> 00:05:06.901
-We always have
microphones here, by the way.

00:05:06.901 --> 00:05:09.601
-Oh, that's what I --
I thought it might have been...

00:05:09.601 --> 00:05:11.100
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:11.100 --> 00:05:14.467
♪ I never meant to
do those things to you ♪

00:05:14.467 --> 00:05:16.334
I never said
I was a good singer.

00:05:16.334 --> 00:05:21.267
♪ And so I have to say
before I go ♪

00:05:21.267 --> 00:05:22.968
[ Laughs ]

00:05:22.968 --> 00:05:27.901
-♪ That I just want you
to know ♪

00:05:27.901 --> 00:05:33.167
♪ I found a reason for me ♪

00:05:33.167 --> 00:05:37.901
♪ To change who
I used to be ♪

00:05:37.901 --> 00:05:44.834
♪ A reason to start over new ♪

00:05:44.834 --> 00:05:49.434
♪ And the reason is you ♪

00:05:49.434 --> 00:05:50.901
-I want to show everyone a clip.

00:05:50.901 --> 00:05:52.767
Here's Raymond Lee in
"Quantum Leap"!

00:05:52.767 --> 00:05:54.868
Take a look at this.

00:05:54.868 --> 00:05:56.934
-You in there, David?
-Yep, yep.

00:05:56.934 --> 00:05:59.501
Just, uh --
Can't rush this sort of thing.

00:05:59.501 --> 00:06:01.234
-First time is always
a little tricky.

00:06:01.234 --> 00:06:02.534
-Mm-hmm.

00:06:02.934 --> 00:06:04.968
Oh, thank God.

00:06:04.968 --> 00:06:06.467
-Are you okay?

00:06:06.467 --> 00:06:08.367
-I'm in a space shuttle.
[ Laughs ]

00:06:08.367 --> 00:06:09.767
-I know.

00:06:09.767 --> 00:06:13.334
-I thought I was supposed to get
pulled back to 2022 when I left.

00:06:13.334 --> 00:06:14.801
-Yeah, that didn't work.

00:06:14.801 --> 00:06:16.000
-Do we know why?

00:06:16.000 --> 00:06:18.300
-We're working on it.

00:06:18.300 --> 00:06:19.767
However,
the team is fairly confident

00:06:19.767 --> 00:06:21.767
we should be able to
get you back on the next leap.

00:06:21.767 --> 00:06:23.234
-Well, I'd might be more upset,

00:06:23.234 --> 00:06:25.434
but...space shuttle.

00:06:25.434 --> 00:06:26.968
It's very cool.

00:06:26.968 --> 00:06:29.300
-That's Raymond Lee, everyone.

00:06:29.300 --> 00:06:32.634
"Quantum Leap" airs
Mondays at 10:00 p.m. on NBC.

